{"id":"35f39a6f1cb082c04c950950","source":"guardian-rss","source_name":"The Guardian World","platform":"rss","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/08/ai-datacentre-firmus-slash-valuation-before-asx-listing","published_at":"2026-10-08T00:57:58Z","collected_at":"2026-10-08T01:14:34.853569Z","title":"Datacentre company Firmus’s high flying valuation may be coming back down to earth ahead of expected ASX debut","text":"Firmus’s plans to list on the ASX on 23 October, in what would have been the largest IPO since Telstra in 1997, are now in doubt. Photograph: PR IMAGE View image in fullscreen Firmus’s plans to list on the ASX on 23 October, in what would have been the largest IPO since Telstra in 1997, are now in doubt. Photograph: PR IMAGE Datacentres - Australia Analysis Datacentre company Firmus’s high flying valuation may be coming back down to earth ahead of expected ASX debut Jonathan Barrett Sources say Firmus is slashing its price and may even shelve initial public offering altogether Get our breaking news email , free app or daily news podcast Wed 7 Oct 2026 20.57 EDT Last modified on Wed 7 Oct 2026 21.10 EDT Share The momentum behind Firmus Technologies’ high-flying valuation is showing severe cracks just weeks out from its anticipated ASX debut. Multiple sources briefed on the matter told Guardian Australia the AI datacentre company is slashing its valuation to entice sceptical investors – or may even shelve its initial public offering altogether. On Thursday, Firmus abruptly withdrew from its scheduled appearance at a parliamentary inquiry into artificial intelligence amid harried disc","html":"","media":["https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/569eb02492eca0edba751bcd408cd19c78468a89/0_0_3000_1582/master/3000.jpg?width=465&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none"],"author":"Jonathan Barrett","language":"und","group":"international-media","perspective":"mixed","trust":"high","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha256":"ba1cdb0ad6c57ebb5cb1005b19aff094116f4c51b69347fe1f1e163259e0e681","original_text_chars":5087,"original_html_chars":19844,"text_truncated":true,"media_count":1,"platform":{"entry_id":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/08/ai-datacentre-firmus-slash-valuation-before-asx-listing","entry_link":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/08/ai-datacentre-firmus-slash-valuation-before-asx-listing"}}}
{"id":"bdeca34bd236c65e58dac5de","source":"guardian-rss","source_name":"The Guardian World","platform":"rss","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/oct/07/donald-trump-gavin-newsom-california-la-san-diego-iran-republicans-democrats-us-politics-latest-news-updates","published_at":"2026-10-08T00:42:51Z","collected_at":"2026-10-08T01:14:48.038249Z","title":"Multiple protesters interrupt Trump as he speaks at Paxton rally in Texas – US politics live","text":"19.49 EDT Trump rally speech in San Antonio interrupted by multiple protesters as he repeats lie about Talarico Donald Trump’s midterm rally speech in San Antonio, Texas has been disrupted by protesters at least six times so far. Protestors were escorted out after disrupting Donald Trump’s speech at the Freeman Coliseum in San Antonio, Texas on Wednesday. Photograph: Win McNamee/Getty Images Television coverage of the rally showed that one of the protesters was violently assaulted by an older Trump supporter as he attempted to leave the arena. A protester wearing a soccer jersey of the Spanish national team was lead out of a campaign rally in San Antonio, Texas, on Wednesday. Photograph: Mandel Ngan/AFP/Getty Images “You know, many of these protesters are paid,” Trump said, repeating a baseless claim he has been making for a decade. “These are paid protesters. They’re paid by enemies of our nation. Now, I’m telling you, they pay them for this. ” A demonstrator holds a Cuban flag as Donald Trump speaks. Photograph: Evan Vucci/Reuters The interruptions seemed to momentarily derail the president as he repeated a lie about James Talarico, the Texas Democrat he claims is a vegan who onl","html":"","media":["https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/07a0ed4831e7521f0fa1af01ecfdcc366bfbc607/0_0_3000_1999/master/3000.jpg?width=465&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none","https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/2650c58d9546cdbe19362a612479ddb789966ce6/0_0_2255_1503/master/2255.jpg?width=465&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none","https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/7475acf236ce35a732d032075c2658f6048fd134/1000_0_5000_4000/master/5000.jpg?width=465&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none"],"author":"Robert Mackey (now); Shrai Popat, Marina Dunbar and Tom Ambrose (earlier)","language":"und","group":"international-media","perspective":"mixed","trust":"high","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha256":"123204d8677b3ca2699ae0c0a31762dd903fb42e973398d8ead3d66ace676237","original_text_chars":2243,"original_html_chars":7955,"text_truncated":true,"media_count":3,"platform":{"entry_id":"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/oct/07/donald-trump-gavin-newsom-california-la-san-diego-iran-republicans-democrats-us-politics-latest-news-updates","entry_link":"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/oct/07/donald-trump-gavin-newsom-california-la-san-diego-iran-republicans-democrats-us-politics-latest-news-updates"}}}
{"id":"fabe853ccb81b5ee0aa0899d","source":"guardian-rss","source_name":"The Guardian World","platform":"rss","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/oct/07/margaret-hamilton-moon-computer-software","published_at":"2026-10-08T00:40:37Z","collected_at":"2026-10-08T01:14:48.248816Z","title":"Margaret Hamilton, trailblazer whose software powered Apollo 11 moon landing, dies at 90","text":"Margaret Hamilton at work in this undated handout photo from the Smithsonian National Air and Space Museum.. Photograph: AFP/Getty Images View image in fullscreen Margaret Hamilton at work in this undated handout photo from the Smithsonian National Air and Space Museum.. Photograph: AFP/Getty Images Space Margaret Hamilton, trailblazer whose software powered Apollo 11 moon landing, dies at 90 MIT computer scientist led development of software for moon mission and earned Presidential Medal of Freedom Uwa Ede-Osifo Wed 7 Oct 2026 20.40 EDT Last modified on Wed 7 Oct 2026 20.42 EDT Share Prefer the Guardian on Google Margaret Hamilton, the computer pioneer whose software powered the first moon landing, has died, the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) announced on Wednesday. She was 90. In an era before titles such as software engineer and computer scientist became mainstream, Hamilton, who died on 30 September, learned to program under the tutelage of a renowned MIT meteorologist. She continued to perfect the craft in an MIT laboratory, writing software that could detect enemy aircraft. When the institute received a Nasa contract to develop the Apollo onboard flight software,","html":"","media":["https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/146bdf84911501986822f5cd74b6789159c42193/22_0_3125_2499/master/3125.jpg?width=465&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none"],"author":"Uwa Ede-Osifo","language":"und","group":"international-media","perspective":"mixed","trust":"high","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha256":"e4ab5d8a2dbfbfef294f4e121b42b9cace951c0c34866d281b4b508f966d0da6","original_text_chars":2625,"original_html_chars":13341,"text_truncated":true,"media_count":1,"platform":{"entry_id":"https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/oct/07/margaret-hamilton-moon-computer-software","entry_link":"https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/oct/07/margaret-hamilton-moon-computer-software"}}}
{"id":"d32dedc48e2bd73c0ec4593e","source":"guardian-rss","source_name":"The Guardian World","platform":"rss","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/07/texas-execution-jamaal-howard","published_at":"2026-10-08T00:13:53Z","collected_at":"2026-10-08T01:14:48.606633Z","title":"Texas set to carry out first US execution since botched lethal injection of Christa Pike","text":"The penitentiary in Livingston, Texas. Photograph: Houston Chronicle/Hearst Newspapers/Getty Images View image in fullscreen The penitentiary in Livingston, Texas. Photograph: Houston Chronicle/Hearst Newspapers/Getty Images Texas Texas set to carry out first US execution since botched lethal injection of Christa Pike Jamaal Howard’s lawyers urged halt, citing risk of another failed execution, but court denied request Uwa Ede-Osifo Wed 7 Oct 2026 20.13 EDT First published on Wed 7 Oct 2026 16.58 EDT Share Prefer the Guardian on Google Texas on Wednesday is scheduled to carry out the first execution in the US after the the botched lethal injection of Christa Pike in Tennessee last week. Lawyers for Jamaal Howard, a Texas man on death row for capital murder, sought to halt the execution, arguing to the Texas court of criminal appeals there are similar risks as in the case of Pike. The court denied the request for a stay and later denied a second attempt to stop the execution over the drug. The court denied both without elaboration. The US supreme court also denied a late appeal Wednesday evening without comment. Judge orders officials to preserve all evidence tied to Christa Pike’s b","html":"","media":["https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/86a22b8783a1593ef64bd36e1567d28411cc110d/0_0_2355_1570/master/2355.jpg?width=465&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none","https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/2c140a5e6648911ff3d720444c02a67ce7040236/0_0_3000_2000/master/3000.jpg?width=445&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none"],"author":"Uwa Ede-Osifo","language":"und","group":"international-media","perspective":"mixed","trust":"high","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha256":"1d055b9c5fb7126c65cdafc43fa65f42c06515a39003f9fa15f721c6284729bb","original_text_chars":3428,"original_html_chars":17479,"text_truncated":true,"media_count":2,"platform":{"entry_id":"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/07/texas-execution-jamaal-howard","entry_link":"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/07/texas-execution-jamaal-howard"}}}
{"id":"d7c00e4db2beb43f756d71de","source":"colonelcassad-tg","source_name":"Boris Rozhin","platform":"telegram","url":"https://t.me/boris_rozhin/228803","published_at":"2026-10-08T00:03:01Z","collected_at":"2026-10-08T01:14:20.625369Z","title":"","text":"⠀ 🔴 Свидетельства вернувшихся из плена о зверствах украинских неонацистов. Смотреть на Rutube Смотреть предыдущие свидетельства Наш Международный общественный трибунал по преступлениям украинских неонацистов (председатель — М. С. Григорьев ) из представителей гражданского общества 35 стран мира продолжает сбор свидетельств преступлений киевского режима. Часть 1 Часть 2. Российский военнослужащий с позывным \"Коба\": 00:35 \"Во время допросов мне угрожали запенить монтажной пеной задний проход и отрезать гениталии. Это была контрразведка. Когда я не отвечал на вопросы, мне ножом разрезали губу. 01:22 Три раза меня хотели зарезать, два застрелить. Во время допросов я молчал, они дважды приставляли нож и надавливали им. Говорили, что хотят вырезать селезёнку. 01:58 Когда меня привезли в госпиталь, спрашивали, употребляю ли я спиртное. Я ответил: \"Вам для чего это знать?\" Мне сказали: \"На продажу пойдёт\". 02:50 Стреляли во время допросов из автоматов, когда ответы пленных не совпадали. Например, если людей из одного полка или одной части спрашивали об одном и том же, а их ответы различались, начинались угрозы и стрельба\". Проект реализуется при поддержке Леонида Слуцкого, Бориса Рожина, А","html":"","media":["https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/RpHCHecQ6oX1JCW-F7YDCODOssrg8gGPmqKzkiQf2Qq0Kv1UY5_Fakl53YAdbE-0ulsctKy7YvjB1qLcPa99fWqJUJJX2bCvz-T1dy7vaQfZFzueE8f4UQTig_zHqCMfPYeOz-Ym61lnGObGh5vyF7Ic-ifltB8h8MNCiUCe_bSltgzmPelBmd46nSUYExEUz1qiR2tan7vW-LEvXRrXoEOnEyIzxlbGPrMAOyjYN9p5k1_rfwkJjLirMzJS47rUK-rRwJto58MxVhI8llY--vEWnHxwATKY9JJP5rvxYPNum2f9mTpai1EY93PBZsccKZOvOQTb2UZk6MjboNQvGw","https://rutube.ru/video/4109f0345bc8c8aefc71895210ffa572/"],"author":"Boris Rozhin","language":"und","group":"ru-milbloggers","perspective":"